modelica://Modelica.Blocks/Sinc:
Modelica.Blocks: Sinc (block)

The Real output y is a sinc signal: amplitude*(sin(2*π*f*t))/((2*π*f*t))

Code:
block Sinc "Generate sinc signal"
  import Modelica.Constants.pi;
  import Modelica.Constants.eps;
  parameter Real amplitude = 1 "Amplitude of sine wave" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency f(start = 1) "Frequency of sine wave";
  extends Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.SignalSource;
protected
  Modelica.Units.SI.Angle x = 2 * pi * f * (time - startTime);
equation
  y = offset + (if time < startTime then 0 else amplitude * (if noEvent(time - startTime < eps) then 1 else sin(x) / x));

end Sinc;

