modelica://Modelica.Clocked/UpSample-5:
Modelica.Clocked: UpSample (block)

This block for Boolean signals works similarly as the corresponding block for Real signals (see  RealSignals.Sampler.Utilities.UpSample ).   
 Analog to the corresponding Real signal block example there exists an elementary example for this Boolean block.

Code:
block UpSample "Upsample the clocked Boolean input signal and provide it as clocked output signal"
  parameter Boolean inferFactor = true "= true, if upsampling factor is inferred" ;
  parameter Integer factor(min = 1) = 1 "Upsampling factor >= 1 (if inferFactor=false)" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.BooleanInput u "Connector of clocked, Boolean input signal" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.BooleanOutput y "Connector of clocked, Boolean output signal (clock of y is faster as clock of u)" ;
protected
  Boolean dummy ;
  Boolean b(start = false);
  Boolean b_super(start = false);
  Boolean u_super;
equation
  when Clock() then
    // clock of u
    dummy = u;
    b = not previous(b);
  end when;
  when Clock() then
    // clock of y
    b_super = superSample(b);
    if inferFactor then
      u_super = superSample(u);
    else
      u_super = superSample(u, factor);
    end if;
    y = if b_super <> previous(b_super) then u_super else false;
  end when;

end UpSample;

