modelica://Modelica.Clocked/UnitDelay-3:
Modelica.Clocked: UnitDelay (block)

This block describes a unit delay:     // Time domain description y(ti) = previous(u(ti)) // Discrete transfer function 1 y(z) = --- * u(z) z   
 that is, the output signal y is the input signal u at the previous clock tick. At the first clock tick, the output y is set to parameter y_start.

Code:
block UnitDelay "Delay the clocked input signal for one sample period"
  extends Modelica.Clocked.BooleanSignals.Interfaces.PartialClockedSISO(u(final start = y_start));
  parameter Boolean y_start = false "Value of output signal at first clock tick";
equation
  y = previous(u);

end UnitDelay;

modelica://Modelica.Clocked/FractionalDe:
Modelica.Clocked: FractionalDelay (block)

Code:
block FractionalDelay "Delay the clocked input signal for a fractional multiple of the sample period"
  extends Modelica.Clocked.BooleanSignals.Interfaces.PartialClockedSISO;
  parameter Integer shift(min = 0) = 0 "Delay = interval() * shift/resolution";
  parameter Integer resolution(min = 1) = 1 "Time quantization resolution of sample interval";
protected
  parameter Integer n = div(shift, resolution);
  Boolean u_buffer[n + 1](each start = false) "The previous values of the inputs; u_last[1] = u, u_last[2] = previous(u_last[1]); u_last[3] = previous(u_last[2])";
  Boolean first(start = true) "Used to identify the first clock tick";
equation
  first = false;
  u_buffer = if previous(first) then fill(u, n + 1) else cat(1, {u}, previous(u_buffer[1:n]));
  y = shiftSample(u_buffer[n + 1], shift, resolution);

end FractionalDelay;

modelica://Modelica.Clocked/ClockToBoole:
Modelica.Clocked: ClockToBoolean (block)

Code:
block ClockToBoolean "Block to translate clock signals to continuous Boolean events (each time the input clock ticks a rising Boolean output edge is produced)."
  extends Modelica.Clocked.ClockSignals.Interfaces.ClockedBlockIcon;
  extends Modelica.Blocks.Icons.PartialBooleanBlock;
  Modelica.Clocked.ClockSignals.Interfaces.ClockInput u "Connector of clock input signal." ;
