modelica://Modelica.ComplexBlocks/Gain:
Modelica.ComplexBlocks: Gain (block)

This block computes output y as  product of gain k with the input u . Optionally, the input u can be processed conjugate complex, when parameter useConjugateInput is true . Depending on useConjugateInput either the original or the conjugate complex input signal are processed.     y = k * (if useConjugateInput then Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(u) else u);   
Example: If useConjugateInput = true and k = 2 the output signal y = 2 * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(u) .

Code:
block Gain "Output the product of a gain value with the input signal"
  parameter Complex k(re(start = 1), im(start = 0)) "Gain value multiplied with input signal";
  parameter Boolean useConjugateInput = false "If true, input is processed conjugate complex";
  Modelica.ComplexBlocks.Interfaces.ComplexInput u "Input signal connector" ;
  Modelica.ComplexBlocks.Interfaces.ComplexOutput y "Output signal connector" ;
equation
  y = k * (if useConjugateInput then Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(u) else u);

</pre></blockquote>
<p><strong>Example:</strong> If <code>useConjugateInput = true</code> and <code>k = 2</code> the output signal <code>y = 2 * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(u)</code>.</p>
