modelica://Modelica.Electrical/Inverting:
Modelica.Electrical: InvertingAmp (model)

This is an inverting amplifier. Resistance R1 can be chosen, R2 is defined by the desired amplification k.

Code:
model InvertingAmp "Inverting amplifier"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage Vps = +15 "Positive supply";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage Vns = -15 "Negative supply";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage Vin = 5 "Amplitude of input voltage";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency f = 10 "Frequency of input voltage";
  parameter Real k = 2 "Desired amplification";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance R1 = 1000 "Arbitrary resistance";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance R2 = k * R1 "Calculated resistance to reach desired amplification k";
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Ideal.IdealOpAmpLimited opAmp(out(i(start = 0, fixed = false))) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.TrapezoidVoltage vIn(V = 2 * Vin, rising = 0.2 / f, width = 0.3 / f, falling = 0.2 / f, period = 1 / f, nperiod = -1, offset = -Vin, startTime = -(vIn.rising + vIn.width / 2)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sensors.VoltageSensor vOut ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor r1(R = R1) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor r2(R = R2) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground1 ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.ConstantVoltage vSourcePos(V = Vps) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.ConstantVoltage vSourceNeg(V = Vns) ;
equation
  connect(r1.n, r2.n) ;
  connect(r2.n, opAmp.in_n) ;
  connect(r2.p, opAmp.out) ;
  connect(ground.p, opAmp.in_p) ;
  connect(vIn.p, r1.p) ;
  connect(ground.p, vIn.n) ;
  connect(ground.p, vOut.n) ;
  connect(opAmp.out, vOut.p) ;
  connect(ground1.p, vSourcePos.n) ;
  connect(vSourcePos.p, opAmp.VMax) ;
  connect(vSourcePos.n, vSourceNeg.n) ;
  connect(vSourceNeg.p, opAmp.VMin) ;

end InvertingAmp;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/SeriesRes:
Modelica.Electrical: SeriesResonance (model)

This model demonstrates the transient behaviour of a series resonant circuit: A sine or cosine voltage with variable frequency and constant amplitude is applied to a series connection of L, C and R. The parameter values result in a resonance frequency of 100 Hz.

Code:
model SeriesResonance "Series resonance circuit"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  import Modelica.Constants.pi;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.SineVoltageVariableFrequencyAndAmplitude sineVoltage(useConstantAmplitude = true, phi(fixed = true)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground1 ;
