modelica://Modelica.Electrical/Different:
Modelica.Electrical: DifferentialAmplifier (model)

This model demonstrates a differential amplifier to attenuate the input voltage to a level that can be handled by the measurement instrument.   
 Two sinusoidal source voltages with a phase shift of 120° (e.g., two phases of a three-phase system) feed a load resistor. The voltage at the load resistor has to be measured but is too high for direct measurement.    Notes  
The output of the amplifier is inverted with respect to the differential input, as well as attenuated by the factor 1/data.k. The influence of the measurement instrument's input resistance on the measurement result is small. The current consumption of the amplifier inputs at the source circuit is small ( resistor1.i and resistor2.i ). The common of the source and the common of the amplifier are connected by a ground resistor. In case this resistance is low, a small current is flowing between the amplifier's common and the source's common ( resistorGround.i ). In case this resistance is high, the amplifier's common is floating with respect to the source's common with a high voltage ( resistorGround.v ).

Code:
model DifferentialAmplifier "Differential amplifier"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  parameter Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Examples.OpAmps.OpAmpCircuits.DifferentialAmplifierData data "Parameters for source, OpAmp and measurement" ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.SineVoltage sourceVoltage1(V = sqrt(2 / 3) * data.VSource, phase = 1.0471975511966, f = data.fSource) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.SineVoltage sourceVoltage2(V = sqrt(2 / 3) * data.VSource, phase = -1.0471975511966, f = data.fSource) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistanceLoad(R = data.RLoad) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sensors.VoltageSensor voltageSensorSource ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Gain gain(k = -1 / data.k) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistorGround(R = data.RGround, i(start = 0, fixed = false)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Ideal.IdealizedOpAmpLimited opAmp(V0 = data.V0, useSupply = true, Vps = +data.VSupply, Vns = -data.VSupply) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor1(R = data.R1, i(start = 0, fixed = false)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor2(R = data.R2, i(start = 0, fixed = false)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor3(R = data.R3) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor4(R = data.R4) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.ConstantVoltage positiveSupply(V = +data.VSupply) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.ConstantVoltage negativeSupply(V = -data.VSupply) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistanceInstrument(R = data.RInstrument) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sensors.VoltageSensor voltageSensor ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.RootMeanSquare rootMeanSquare(f = data.fSource) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground ;
protected
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Interfaces.NegativePin groundSource "Negative electrical pin" ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Interfaces.NegativePin groundOpAmp "Negative electrical pin" ;
equation
  connect(voltageSensor.v, rootMeanSquare.u) ;
  connect(resistor4.n, groundOpAmp) ;
  connect(groundOpAmp, resistorGround.n) ;
  connect(groundOpAmp, resistanceInstrument.n) ;
  connect(groundOpAmp, voltageSensor.n) ;
  connect(groundOpAmp, positiveSupply.n) ;
  connect(groundOpAmp, negativeSupply.n) ;
  connect(negativeSupply.p, opAmp.s_n) ;
  connect(opAmp.s_p, positiveSupply.p) ;
  connect(sourceVoltage1.n, groundSource) ;
  connect(groundSource, sourceVoltage2.n) ;
  connect(groundSource, resistorGround.p) ;
  connect(groundSource, ground.p) ;
  connect(sourceVoltage1.p, resistor1.p) ;
  connect(sourceVoltage2.p, resistor2.p) ;
  connect(voltageSensorSource.v, gain.u) ;
  connect(sourceVoltage2.p, voltageSensorSource.n) ;
  connect(sourceVoltage1.p, voltageSensorSource.p) ;
  connect(sourceVoltage1.p, resistanceLoad.p) ;
  connect(sourceVoltage2.p, resistanceLoad.n) ;
  connect(resistor3.n, resistanceInstrument.p) ;
  connect(resistor3.n, voltageSensor.p) ;
  connect(resistor3.n, opAmp.out) ;
  connect(resistor1.n, resistor3.p) ;
  connect(resistor2.n, resistor4.p) ;
  connect(resistor2.n, opAmp.in_p) ;
  connect(resistor1.n, opAmp.in_n) ;

end DifferentialAmplifier;

