modelica://Modelica.Electrical/SineVolta:
Modelica.Electrical: SineVoltageVariableFrequencyAndAmplitude (model)

This voltage source provides a sinusoidal voltage with variable frequency f and variable amplitude V , i.e. the phase angle of the sine wave is integrated from 2*π*f.   
 Note that the initial value of the phase angle phi defines the initial phase shift, and that the parameter startTime is omitted since the voltage can be kept equal to offset with setting the input V to zero.

Code:
model SineVoltageVariableFrequencyAndAmplitude "Sine voltage source with variable frequency and amplitude"
  extends Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Interfaces.OnePort;
  extends Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Icons.VoltageSource;
  import Modelica.Constants.pi;
  parameter Boolean useConstantAmplitude = false "Enable constant amplitude";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage constantAmplitude = 1 "Constant amplitude" ;
  parameter Boolean useConstantFrequency = false "Enable constant frequency";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency constantFrequency = 1 "Constant frequency" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage offset = 0 "Offset of the sine wave";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Angle phi(start = 0) "Phase of the sine wave";
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput V(unit = "V") if not useConstantAmplitude "Amplitude" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput f(unit = "Hz") if not useConstantFrequency "Frequency" ;
protected
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput V_internal(unit = "V") "Amplitude" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput f_internal(unit = "Hz") "Frequency" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Constant V_constant(final k = constantAmplitude) if useConstantAmplitude ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Constant f_constant(final k = constantFrequency) if useConstantFrequency ;
equation
  der(phi) = 2 * pi * f_internal;
  v = offset + V_internal * sin(phi);
  connect(f, f_internal) ;
  connect(V, V_internal) ;
  connect(f_constant.y, f_internal) ;
  connect(V_constant.y, V_internal) ;

end SineVoltageVariableFrequencyAndAmplitude;

