modelica://Modelica.Electrical/CurrentCo:
Modelica.Electrical: CurrentControlledDCPM (model)

This model demonstrates how a current controller for a DC PM drive works.  
 The current controller is parameterized according to the absolute optimum.   
At time=0.2 s a reference torque step is applied, causing the drive to accelerate until motor torque and load torque are at an equilibrium.  
 Further reading:  Tutorial at the Modelica Conference 2017

Code:
model CurrentControlledDCPM "Current controlled DC PM drive with H-bridge from battery"
  extends Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.PartialControlledDCPM;
  Modelica.Mechanics.Rotational.Sources.QuadraticSpeedDependentTorque loadTorque(tau_nominal = -driveData.tauNominal, TorqueDirection = false, w_nominal = driveData.motorData.wNominal) ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Step step(offset = 0, startTime = 0.2, height = driveData.tauNominal) ;
equation
  connect(loadInertia.flange_b, loadTorque.flange) ;
  connect(step.y, tau2i.u) ;

end CurrentControlledDCPM;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/SpeedCont:
Modelica.Electrical: SpeedControlledDCPM (model)

This model demonstrates how a speed controller for a current controlled DC PM drive works.  
 The inner current controller is parameterized according to the absolute optimum. The outer control loop is formed by the speed controller which is parameterized according to the symmetrical optimum.   
 At time=0.2 s a reference speed step is applied, causing the drive to accelerate to the desired speed. At time=0.8 s a load torque step is applied, causing the drive to decelerate until the speed controller brings the drive back to the desired speed.   
 You may try a slewRateLimiter instead of the prefilter to limit the speed rise i.e. the torque.   
 Further reading:  Tutorial at the Modelica Conference 2017

Code:
model SpeedControlledDCPM "Speed controlled DC PM drive with H-bridge from battery"
  extends Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.PartialControlledDCPM;
  Modelica.Mechanics.Rotational.Sources.TorqueStep loadTorque(stepTorque = -driveData.tauNominal, offsetTorque = 0, startTime = 0.8) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.LimitedPI speedController(initType = Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init.InitialOutput, k = driveData.kpw, Ti = driveData.Tiw, constantLimits = true, yMax = driveData.tauMax) ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Continuous.FirstOrder preFilter(k = 1, T = driveData.Tfw, initType = Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init.InitialOutput) ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Step step(offset = 0, height = driveData.motorData.wNominal, startTime = 0.2) ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Nonlinear.SlewRateLimiter slewRateLimiter(initType = Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init.InitialOutput, Rising = driveData.aMax) ;
equation
  connect(step.y, preFilter.u) ;
  connect(loadInertia.flange_b, loadTorque.flange) ;
  connect(speedSensor.w, speedController.u_m) ;
  connect(speedController.y, tau2i.u) ;
  connect(step.y, slewRateLimiter.u) ;
  connect(speedController.u, preFilter.y) ;

end SpeedControlledDCPM;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/PositionC:
Modelica.Electrical: PositionControlledDCPM (model)

This model demonstrates how a position controller for a speed controlled DC PM drive works.  
 The inner current controller is parameterized according to the absolute optimum. The middle control loop is formed by the speed controller which is parameterized according to the symmetrical optimum. The outer control loop is formed by the position controller which is parameterized to avoid an overshot in the position.   
 At time=0.2 s the kinematicPTP starts to prescribe the reference position with limited speed and limited acceleration. At time=2.3 s a load torque step is applied, causing the drive to slightly leave the end position until the position controller brings the drive back to the desired position.   
 Further reading:  Tutorial at the Modelica Conference 2017

Code:
model PositionControlledDCPM "Position controlled DC PM drive with H-bridge from battery"
  extends Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.PartialControlledDCPM;
  Modelica.Mechanics.Rotational.Sources.TorqueStep loadTorque(stepTorque = -driveData.tauNominal, offsetTorque = 0, startTime = 2.3) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.LimitedPI speedController(initType = Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init.InitialOutput, k = driveData.kpw, Ti = driveData.Tiw, constantLimits = true, yMax = driveData.tauMax) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.LimitedPI positionController(constantLimits = true, k = driveData.kpP, useI = false, yMax = driveData.wMax, initType = Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init.SteadyState) ;
  Modelica.Mechanics.Rotational.Sensors.AngleSensor angleSensor ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.KinematicPTP2 kinematicPTP(qd_max = {driveData.wMax}, qdd_max = {driveData.aMax}, q_end = {200}, startTime = 0.2) ;
equation
  connect(positionController.y, speedController.u) ;
  connect(angleSensor.phi, positionController.u_m) ;
  connect(kinematicPTP.q[1], positionController.u) ;
  connect(speedSensor.flange, angleSensor.flange) ;
  connect(speedSensor.w, speedController.u_m) ;
  connect(loadInertia.flange_b, loadTorque.flange) ;
  connect(speedController.y, tau2i.u) ;

end PositionControlledDCPM;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/PartialCo:
Modelica.Electrical: PartialControlledDCPM (model)

This is a partial model of a controlled DC PM drive.  
 Electrical power is taken from a battery (constant voltage with inner resistance) and fed to the motor via a DC-DC inverter. The level of detail of the DC-DC inverter may be chosen from ideal averaging or switching. The DC-DC inverter is commanded by the current controller. The current controller is parameterized according to the absolute optimum.   
 Further reading:  Tutorial at the Modelica Conference 2017

Code:
partial model PartialControlledDCPM "Partial controlled DC PM drive with H-bridge from battery"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  replaceable parameter Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.DriveDataDCPM driveData constrainedby ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.DriveDataDCPM "DC machine data" ;
  Modelica.Mechanics.Rotational.Components.Inertia loadInertia(J = driveData.JL) ;
  Modelica.Mechanics.Rotational.Sensors.SpeedSensor speedSensor ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Machines.BasicMachines.DCMachines.DC_PermanentMagnet dcpm(TaOperational = driveData.motorData.TaNominal, VaNominal = driveData.motorData.VaNominal, IaNominal = driveData.motorData.IaNominal, wNominal = driveData.motorData.wNominal, TaNominal = driveData.motorData.TaNominal, Ra = driveData.motorData.Ra, TaRef = driveData.motorData.TaRef, La = driveData.motorData.La, Jr = driveData.motorData.Jr, frictionParameters = driveData.motorData.frictionParameters, phiMechanical(fixed = true), wMechanical(fixed = true), coreParameters = driveData.motorData.coreParameters, strayLoadParameters = driveData.motorData.strayLoadParameters, brushParameters = driveData.motorData.brushParameters, ia(fixed = true), Js = driveData.motorData.Js, alpha20a = driveData.motorData.alpha20a) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.DcdcInverter armatureInverter(fS = driveData.fS, Td = driveData.Td, Tmf = driveData.Tmf, VMax = driveData.VaMax) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.Battery source(INominal = driveData.motorData.IaNominal, V0 = driveData.VBat) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Examples.ControlledDCDrives.Utilities.LimitedPI currentController(constantLimits = false, k = driveData.kpI, Ti = driveData.TiI, KFF = driveData.kPhi, initType = Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init.InitialOutput, useFF = true) ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Gain tau2i(k = 1 / driveData.kPhi) ;
equation
  connect(dcpm.flange, loadInertia.flange_a) ;
  connect(speedSensor.flange, dcpm.flange) ;
  connect(armatureInverter.pin_nMot, dcpm.pin_an) ;
  connect(armatureInverter.pin_pMot, dcpm.pin_ap) ;
  connect(armatureInverter.vDC, currentController.yMaxVar) ;
  connect(armatureInverter.vRef, currentController.y) ;
  connect(armatureInverter.iMot, currentController.u_m) ;
  connect(speedSensor.w, currentController.feedForward) ;
  connect(tau2i.y, currentController.u) ;
  connect(source.pin_n, armatureInverter.pin_nBat) ;
  connect(source.pin_p, armatureInverter.pin_pBat) ;

end PartialControlledDCPM;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/DriveData:
Modelica.Electrical: DriveDataDCPM (record)

Calculates controller parameters of a DC permanent magnet drive: Current controller according to absolute optimum, speed controller according to symmetric optimum.

Code:
record DriveDataDCPM "Parameters of a controlled DC permanent magnet drive"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Record;
  import Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Thermal.convertResistance;
  //Motor
  parameter Modelica.Electrical.Machines.Utilities.ParameterRecords.DcPermanentMagnetData motorData "Motor data" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance Ra = convertResistance(motorData.Ra, motorData.TaRef, motorData.alpha20a, motorData.TaNominal) "Armature resistance at nominal temperature" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time Ta = motorData.La / Ra "Armature time constant" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Power PNominal = motorData.ViNominal * motorData.IaNominal - motorData.frictionParameters.PRef - motorData.coreParameters.PRef - motorData.strayLoadParameters.PRef "Nominal mechanical output" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Torque tauNominal = PNominal / motorData.wNominal "Nominal torque" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.ElectricalTorqueConstant kPhi = tauNominal / motorData.IaNominal "Torque constant" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.AngularVelocity w0 = motorData.wNominal * motorData.VaNominal / motorData.ViNominal "No-load speed" ;
  //Inverter
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency fS = 2e3 "Switching frequency" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage VBat = VaMax "DC no-load voltage" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time Td = 0.5 / fS "Dead time of inverter" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time Tmf = 4 * Td "Measurement filter time constant" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time Tsigma = Td + Tmf "Sum of small time constants" ;
  //Load
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Inertia JL = motorData.Jr "Load inertia" ;
  //Limits
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage VaMax = 1.2 * motorData.VaNominal "Maximum Voltage" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Current IaMax = 1.5 * motorData.IaNominal "Maximum current" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Torque tauMax = kPhi * IaMax "Maximum torque" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.AngularVelocity wMax = motorData.wNominal * motorData.VaNominal / motorData.ViNominal "Maximum speed" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.AngularAcceleration aMax = tauMax / (JL + motorData.Jr) "Maximum acceleration" ;
  //Current controller: absolute optimum
  parameter Real kpI = motorData.La / (2 * Tsigma) "Proportional gain" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time TiI = Ta "Integral time constant" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time Tsub = 2 * Tsigma "Substitute time constant" ;
  //Speed controller: symmetrical optimum
  parameter Real kpw = (JL + motorData.Jr) / (2 * Tsub) "Proportional gain" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time Tiw = 4 * Tsub "Integral time constant" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time Tfw = Tiw "Filter time constant" ;
  //Position controller
  parameter Real kpP = 1 / (16 * Tsub) "Proportional gain" ;

end DriveDataDCPM;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/LimitedPI:
Modelica.Electrical: LimitedPI (block)

Proportional - Integral - controller with optional feed-forward and limitation at the output.   
 The integral part can be switched off to obtain a limited P-controller.   
 The feed-forward gain can either be constant or given by the optional input kFF.   
 When the output is limited, the controller cannot bring the control error to zero and the integrator will not stop integrating. To avoid this WindUp - effect, an Anti-WindUp loop is implemented: The difference between unlimited and limited output is fed back to the integrator's input.

Code:
block LimitedPI "Limited PI-controller with anti-windup and feed-forward"
  extends Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.SISO;
  import Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init;
  import Modelica.Constants.inf;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput u_m "Connector of measured signal" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput feedForward if useFF "Connector of feed-forward signal" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput kFF if useFF and not useConstantKFF "Connector of feed-forward factor" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput yMaxVar if not constantLimits "Connector of yMax input signal" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput yMinVar if not constantLimits and not symmetricLimits "Connector of yMin input signal" ;
  output Real controlError = u - u_m "Control error (set point - measurement)";
  parameter Real k = 1 "Gain";
  parameter Boolean useI = true "PI else P" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Time Ti(min = Modelica.Constants.small) = 1 "Integral time constant (T>0 required)" ;
  parameter Boolean useFF = false "Use feed-forward?" ;
  parameter Boolean useConstantKFF = true "Use constant feed-forward factor?" ;
  parameter Real KFF = 1 "Feed-forward gain" ;
  parameter Boolean constantLimits = true "Use constant limits?" ;
  parameter Boolean symmetricLimits = true "Use symmetric limits?" ;
  parameter Real yMax = inf "Upper limit of output" ;
  parameter Real yMin = -yMax "Lower limit of output" ;
  parameter Init initType = Init.NoInit "Type of initialization (1: no init, 2: steady state, 3: initial state, 4: initial output)" ;
  parameter Real x_start = 0 "Initial or guess value of state" ;
  parameter Real y_start = 0 "Initial value of output" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Feedback feedback ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Add addAntiWindup(k1 = 1, k2 = -1 / k) ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Continuous.Integrator integrator(k = 1 / Ti, initType = Init.NoInit) if useI ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Add3 add3(k1 = k, k2 = k, k3 = 1) ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Nonlinear.VariableLimiter variableLimiter ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Feedback addSat ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Product product ;
protected
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Constant zeroI(k = 0) if not useI ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Constant zeroFF(k = 0) if not useFF ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Constant constantKFF(k = KFF) if not useFF or useConstantKFF ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Constant yMaxConst(k = yMax) if constantLimits ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Sources.Constant yMinConst(k = yMin) if constantLimits and not symmetricLimits ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Gain gain(k = -1) if symmetricLimits ;
initial equation
  if initType == Init.SteadyState and useI then
    der(add3.u2) = 0;
  elseif initType == Init.InitialState and useI then
    add3.u2 = x_start;
  elseif initType == Init.InitialOutput then
    add3.y = y_start;
  end if;
equation
  connect(addAntiWindup.y, integrator.u) ;
  connect(integrator.y, add3.u2) ;
  connect(add3.y, variableLimiter.u) ;
  connect(variableLimiter.y, y) ;
  connect(add3.y, addSat.u1) ;
  connect(variableLimiter.y, addSat.u2) ;
  connect(add3.u2, zeroI.y) ;
  connect(u, feedback.u1) ;
  connect(feedback.y, add3.u1) ;
  connect(feedback.y, addAntiWindup.u1) ;
  connect(u_m, feedback.u2) ;
  connect(addSat.y, addAntiWindup.u2) ;
  connect(yMinVar, variableLimiter.limit2) ;
  connect(variableLimiter.limit2, yMinConst.y) ;
  connect(yMaxVar, variableLimiter.limit1) ;
  connect(variableLimiter.limit1, yMaxConst.y) ;
  connect(variableLimiter.limit2, gain.y) ;
  connect(variableLimiter.limit1, gain.u) ;
  connect(product.y, add3.u3) ;
  connect(feedForward, product.u1) ;
  connect(product.u1, zeroFF.y) ;
  connect(constantKFF.y, product.u2) ;
  connect(product.u2, kFF) ;

end LimitedPI;

