modelica://Modelica.Electrical/activePow:
Modelica.Electrical: activePower (function)

Transformation of three-phase voltages and currents to space phasors and calculate active power.

Code:
function activePower "Calculate active power of voltage and current input"
  import Modelica.Constants.pi;
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage v[m] "Phase voltages";
  input Modelica.Units.SI.Current i[m] "Phase currents";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power p "Active power";
protected
  constant Integer m = 3 "Number of phases";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage v_[2] "Voltage space phasor";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Current i_[2] "Current space phasor";
algorithm
  v_ := zeros(2);
  i_ := zeros(2);
  for k in 1:m loop
    v_ := v_ + 2 / m * {+cos((k - 1) / m * 2 * pi), +sin(+(k - 1) / m * 2 * pi)} * v[k];
    i_ := i_ + 2 / m * {+cos((k - 1) / m * 2 * pi), +sin(+(k - 1) / m * 2 * pi)} * i[k];
  end for;
  p := m / 2 * (+v_[1] * i_[1] + v_[2] * i_[2]);

end activePower;

