Modelica.Electrical: TransformerYY (model)

Test example with polyphase components:
 Star-connected voltage source feeds via a Y-Y-transformer with internal impedance (RT, LT) a load resistor RT.
 Using f=5 Hz LT=3mH defines nominal voltage drop of approximately 10 %.
 Simulate for 1 second (2 periods) and compare voltages and currents of source, transformer and load.

Code:
model TransformerYY "Test example with polyphase components"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  parameter Integer m = 3 "Number of phases" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage V = 1 "Amplitude of Star-Voltage";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency f = 5 "Frequency";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Inductance Lm = 1 "Transformer main inductance";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Inductance LT = 0.003 "Transformer stray inductance";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance RT = 0.05 "Transformer resistance";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance RL = 1 "Load Resistance";
  parameter Real nT = 1 "Transformer ratio";
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Sources.SineVoltage sineVoltage(V = fill(V, m), f = fill(f, m), m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Star starS(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground groundS ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Ideal.IdealTransformer idealTransformer(m = m, Lm1 = fill(Lm, m), n = fill(nT, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Star starT1(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Star starT2(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground groundT2 ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor transformerR(m = m, R = fill(RT, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Inductor transformerL(m = m, L = fill(LT, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor loadR(m = m, R = fill(RL, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Star starL(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground groundT1 ;
initial equation
  transformerL.i[1:m - 1] = zeros(m - 1) "Y-connection";
equation
  connect(starS.pin_n, groundS.p) ;
  connect(starT1.pin_n, groundT1.p) ;
  connect(starT2.pin_n, groundT2.p) ;
  connect(starS.plug_p, sineVoltage.plug_n) ;
  connect(sineVoltage.plug_p, idealTransformer.plug_p1) ;
  connect(idealTransformer.plug_n1, starT1.plug_p) ;
  connect(starT2.plug_p, idealTransformer.plug_n2) ;
  connect(idealTransformer.plug_p2, transformerR.plug_p) ;
  connect(transformerR.plug_n, transformerL.plug_p) ;
  connect(transformerL.plug_n, loadR.plug_p) ;
  connect(loadR.plug_n, starL.plug_p) ;

end TransformerYY;

