modelica://Modelica.Electrical/Filter:
Modelica.Electrical: Filter (block)

First order filter with cut-off frequency fCut . The phase shift of the filter is compensated by a series of two first order all-pass filters tuned on supply frequency f .

Code:
block Filter "PT1 + all-pass filter"
  extends Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.SISO;
  import Modelica.Constants.pi;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency f = 50 "Mains Frequency";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency fCut = 2 * f "Cut off frequency";
  final parameter Integer na(final min = 2) = 2 "Count of 1st order all-pass";
  final parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency fa = f / tan(pi / na - atan(f / fCut) / (2 * na)) "Characteristic frequency of all-pass filter";
  parameter Real yStart = 0 "Start value of output";
  Modelica.Blocks.Continuous.FirstOrder firstOrder(final k = 1, final T = 1 / (2 * pi * fCut), initType = Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init.InitialOutput, y_start = yStart) ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Continuous.TransferFunction transferFunction[na](each final b = {-1 / (2 * pi * fa), 1}, each final a = {+1 / (2 * pi * fa), 1}, each initType = Modelica.Blocks.Types.Init.InitialOutput, each y_start = yStart) ;
equation
  for j in 1:na - 1 loop
    connect(transferFunction[j].y, transferFunction[j + 1].u);
  end for;
  connect(u, firstOrder.u) ;
  connect(firstOrder.y, transferFunction[1].u) ;
  connect(transferFunction[na].y, y) ;

end Filter;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/SinglePha:
Modelica.Electrical: SinglePhase2Level (model)

This is a single-phase two level inverter. The boolean signals fire_p and fire_n shall not be true at the same time to avoid DC bus short circuits. The inverter consists of two transistors and two anti parallel free wheeling diodes.   
 An example of a single-phase inverter with PWM voltage control is included in  Examples.DCAC.SinglePhaseTwoLevel .

Code:
model SinglePhase2Level "Single-phase DC to AC converter"
  extends Modelica.Blocks.Icons.Block;
