modelica://Modelica.Electrical/MutualInd:
Modelica.Electrical: MutualInductor (model)

Model of a polyphase inductor providing a mutual inductance matrix model.    Implementation    v[1] = j*omega*L[1,1]*i[1] + j*omega*L[1,2]*i[2] + ... + j*omega*L[1,m]*i[m] v[2] = j*omega*L[2,1]*i[1] + j*omega*L[2,2]*i[2] + ... + j*omega*L[2,m]*i[m] : : : : v[m] = j*omega*L[m,1]*i[1] + j*omega*L[m,2]*i[2] + ... + j*omega*L[m,m]*i[m]

Code:
model MutualInductor "Linear mutual inductor"
  extends Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Interfaces.OnePort;
  import Modelica.ComplexMath.j;
  parameter Real epsilon = 1e-9 "Relative accuracy tolerance of matrix symmetry";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Inductance L[m, m] "Mutual inductance matrix";
initial equation
  if abs(Modelica.Math.Matrices.det(L)) < epsilon then
    Modelica.Utilities.Streams.print("Warning: mutual inductance matrix singular!");
  end if;
equation
  assert(sum(abs(L - transpose(L))) < epsilon * sum(abs(L)), "Mutual inductance matrix is not symmetric");
  for l in 1:m loop
    v[l] = sum(j * omega * L[l, k] * i[k] for k in 1:m);
  end for;

end MutualInductor;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/Impedance:
