modelica://Modelica.Electrical/quasiRMS-:
Modelica.Electrical: quasiRMS (function)

This function determines the continuous quasi RMS value of a polyphase system, represented by m quasi-static time domain phasors.

Code:
function quasiRMS "Overall quasi-RMS value of complex input (current or voltage)"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  import Modelica.ComplexMath.abs;
  input Complex u[:];
  output Real y;
  import Modelica.Constants.pi;
protected
  Integer m = size(u, 1) "Number of phases";
algorithm
  // y := sum({abs(u[k]) for k in 1:m})/m;
  // Alternative implementation due to https://trac.openmodelica.org/OpenModelica/ticket/4496
  y := sum(array(sqrt(u[k].re ^ 2 + u[k].im ^ 2) for k in 1:m)) / m;

end quasiRMS;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/activePow:
Modelica.Electrical: activePower (function)

Calculates instantaneous power from polyphase voltages and currents. In quasi-static operation, instantaneous power equals active power;

Code:
function activePower "Calculate active power of complex input voltage and current"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexVoltage v[:] "QuasiStatic voltage phasors";
  input Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexCurrent i[size(v, 1)] "QuasiStatic current phasors";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power p "Active power";
algorithm
  p := sum(Modelica.ComplexMath.real(array(v[k] * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(i[k]) for k in 1:size(v, 1))));

end activePower;

