Code:
partial model TwoPlug "Two plugs with pin-adapter, reference connection and declaration of voltage and current"
  extends Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Interfaces.TwoPlugElementary;
  Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexVoltage v[m] "Complex voltage";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage abs_v[m] = Modelica.ComplexMath.abs(v) "Magnitude of complex voltage";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Angle arg_v[m] = Modelica.ComplexMath.arg(v) "Argument of complex voltage";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexCurrent i[m] "Complex current";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Current abs_i[m] = Modelica.ComplexMath.abs(i) "Magnitude of complex current";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Angle arg_i[m] = Modelica.ComplexMath.arg(i) "Argument of complex current";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ActivePower P[m] = array(Modelica.ComplexMath.real(v[k] * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(i[k])) for k in 1:m) "Active power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ActivePower P_total = sum(P) "Total active power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ReactivePower Q[m] = array(Modelica.ComplexMath.imag(v[k] * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(i[k])) for k in 1:m) "Reactive power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ReactivePower Q_total = sum(Q) "Total reactive power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ApparentPower S[m] = array(Modelica.ComplexMath.abs(v[k] * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(i[k])) for k in 1:m) "Magnitude of complex apparent power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ApparentPower S_total = sqrt(P_total ^ 2 + Q_total ^ 2) "Magnitude of total complex apparent power";
  Real pf[m] = array(cos(Modelica.ComplexMath.arg(Complex(P[k], Q[k]))) for k in 1:m) "Power factor";
  /*
  Real pf_total = cos(Modelica.ComplexMath.arg(Complex(P_total,Q_total)))
   "Total power factor";
  */
equation
  v = plug_p.pin.v - plug_n.pin.v;
  i = plug_p.pin.i;

end TwoPlug;

modelica://Modelica.Electrical/OnePort-4:
Modelica.Electrical: OnePort (model)

This partial model uses a positive  and negative plug and defines the complex voltage differences as well as the complex currents (into the positive plug). A positive and a negative adapter  are used to give easy access to the single pins of both plugs. Additionally, the angular velocity of the quasi-static system is explicitly defined as variable. This model is mainly intended to be used with textual representation of user models.    See also  
  PositivePlug ,  NegativePlug ,  TwoPlug ,  OnePort

Code:
partial model OnePort "Two plugs, reference connection and declaration of voltage and current"
  parameter Integer m(min = 1) = 3 "Number of phases" ;
  Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexVoltage v[m] "Complex voltage";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage abs_v[m] = Modelica.ComplexMath.abs(v) "Magnitude of complex voltage";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Angle arg_v[m] = Modelica.ComplexMath.arg(v) "Argument of complex voltage";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexCurrent i[m] "Complex current";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Current abs_i[m] = Modelica.ComplexMath.abs(i) "Magnitude of complex current";
  Modelica.Units.SI.Angle arg_i[m] = Modelica.ComplexMath.arg(i) "Argument of complex current";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ActivePower P[m] = array(Modelica.ComplexMath.real(v[k] * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(i[k])) for k in 1:m) "Active power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ActivePower P_total = sum(P) "Total active power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ReactivePower Q[m] = array(Modelica.ComplexMath.imag(v[k] * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(i[k])) for k in 1:m) "Reactive power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ReactivePower Q_total = sum(Q) "Total reactive power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ApparentPower S[m] = array(Modelica.ComplexMath.abs(v[k] * Modelica.ComplexMath.conj(i[k])) for k in 1:m) "Magnitude of complex apparent power";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ApparentPower S_total = sqrt(P_total ^ 2 + Q_total ^ 2) "Magnitude of total complex apparent power";
  Real pf[m] = array(cos(Modelica.ComplexMath.arg(Complex(P[k], Q[k]))) for k in 1:m) "Power factor";
  /*
  Real pf_total = cos(Modelica.ComplexMath.arg(Complex(P_total,Q_total)))
    "Total power factor";
  */
  Modelica.Units.SI.AngularVelocity omega "Angular velocity of reference frame";
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Interfaces.PositivePlug plug_p(final m = m) "Positive quasi-static polyphase plug" ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Interfaces.NegativePlug plug_n(final m = m) "Negative quasi-static polyphase plug" ;
equation
  Connections.branch(plug_p.reference, plug_n.reference);
  plug_p.reference.gamma = plug_n.reference.gamma;
  omega = der(plug_p.reference.gamma);
  v = plug_p.pin.v - plug_n.pin.v;
  i = plug_p.pin.i;
  plug_p.pin.i + plug_n.pin.i = fill(Complex(0), m);

end OnePort;

