modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/InductorWit:
Modelica.Magnetic: InductorWithHysteresis (model)

This is a simple model of an inductor with a ferromagnetic core. The used GenericHystTellinenEverett model considers the ferromagnetic hysteresis, eddy currents and remanence of the core material. For example you can simulate the model for 0.02s and plot Core.B vs. Core.H to visualize the resulting hysteresis loops.    Fig. 1: Results Core.B(t) and Core.B(H) of the magnetic Core.

Code:
model InductorWithHysteresis
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Basic.Ground mag_ground ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Basic.ElectroMagneticConverterWithLeakageInductance winding(i(fixed = true), N = 10) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground el_ground ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor(R = 0.1) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.SineVoltage vSource(f = 200, V = 5) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Shapes.HysteresisAndMagnets.GenericHystTellinenEverett core(mat = Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Material.HysteresisEverettParameter.M330_50A(), A = 4e-4, MagRel(fixed = true, start = 0), includeEddyCurrents = true, derHstat(fixed = true), l = 0.1) ;
equation
  connect(winding.port_n, mag_ground.port) ;
  connect(vSource.p, resistor.p) ;
  connect(vSource.n, el_ground.p) ;
  connect(winding.n, el_ground.p) ;
  connect(resistor.n, winding.p) ;
  connect(winding.port_p, core.port_p) ;
  connect(mag_ground.port, core.port_n) ;

end InductorWithHysteresis;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/SinglePhase:
Modelica.Magnetic: SinglePhaseTransformerWithHysteresis1 (model)

This simple model of an single-phase transformer shows the inrush currents due to the remanence of the core material (M330-50A). For an accurate modelling of the core material the GenericHystTellinenTable hysteresis flux tube element is used. The initial magnetization MagRel of the Core component is set to 80%. Simulation settings:   
Stop time: 0.02 s Number of intervals: 5000 Tolerance: 1e-6  
 Then plot the flux density of the Core Core.B over the magnetic field strength Core.H and additionally the time course of the primary and secondary current and e.g. the power consumption of the iron core Core.LossPower (see the following figures).

Code:
model SinglePhaseTransformerWithHysteresis1
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Basic.Ground mag_ground ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Basic.ElectroMagneticConverterWithLeakageInductance winding1(N = 10, i(fixed = true)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground el_ground1 ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor1(R = 0.05) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.SineVoltage vSource(f = 400, V = 8) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Basic.ElectroMagneticConverterWithLeakageInductance winding2(N = 10, i(fixed = true)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor2(R = 2) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground el_ground2 ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Shapes.HysteresisAndMagnets.GenericHystTellinenTable core(asc(fixed = false), mat = Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Material.HysteresisTableData.M330_50A(), includeEddyCurrents = true, l = 0.2, A = 5e-4, MagRel(start = 0.5, fixed = true)) ;
initial equation
  core.derHstat = 0.0;
equation
  connect(winding1.port_n, mag_ground.port) ;
  connect(vSource.p, resistor1.p) ;
  connect(vSource.n, el_ground1.p) ;
  connect(winding1.n, el_ground1.p) ;
  connect(resistor1.n, winding1.p) ;
  connect(winding2.port_n, mag_ground.port) ;
  connect(winding2.p, resistor2.p) ;
  connect(winding2.n, el_ground2.p) ;
  connect(resistor2.n, el_ground2.p) ;
  connect(winding1.port_p, core.port_p) ;
  connect(core.port_n, winding2.port_p) ;

end SinglePhaseTransformerWithHysteresis1;

Modelica.Magnetic: SinglePhaseTransformerWithHysteresis2 (model)

A simple model of an single-phase transformer (similar to SinglePhaseTransformerWithHysteresis1 but with separate transformer model: Transformer1PhaseWithHysteresis ). Use the simulation settings:   
Stop time: 0.1 s Number of intervals: 5000.  
 The figure shows the magnetic hysteresis in the transformer core. In (a) the consideration of the eddy currents is switched off, in (b) it is enabled.

Code:
model SinglePhaseTransformerWithHysteresis2
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground el_ground1 ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor1(R = 0.05) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Sources.SineVoltage SineVoltage(f = 400, V = 6) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor2(R = 2) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground el_ground2 ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Examples.Hysteresis.Components.Transformer1PhaseWithHysteresis transformer(mat = Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Material.HysteresisEverettParameter.M330_50A(), MagRelFixed = true, I1Fixed = true, EddyCurrents = false, HFixed = false) ;
initial equation
  transformer.core.derHstat = 0.0;
equation
  connect(SineVoltage.p, resistor1.p) ;
  connect(SineVoltage.n, el_ground1.p) ;
  connect(resistor2.n, el_ground2.p) ;
  connect(resistor1.n, transformer.p1) ;
  connect(transformer.n1, el_ground1.p) ;
  connect(transformer.p2, resistor2.p) ;
  connect(transformer.n2, el_ground2.p) ;

end SinglePhaseTransformerWithHysteresis2;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/ThreePhaseT:
Modelica.Magnetic: ThreePhaseTransformerWithRectifier (model)

This is a model of a three-phase transformer and rectifier unit using the Transformer3PhaseYyWithHysteresis model. Use the following simulation settings:   
Stop time: 0.2 s Number of intervals: 5000 Tolerance: 1e-6  
 An example simulation shows the transformer inrush currents due to an initially magnetized transformer core.    Fig. 1: Transformer inrush currents due to initial magnetization of the magnetic core; (a) transformer primary currents; (b) transformer secondary currents; (c) flux densities of the transformer legs; (d) B(H) hysteresis loops of transformer leg one.; (e) instantaneous static hysteresis, eddy current and copper losses of the transformer; (f) approximated average static hysteresis, eddy current and copper losses of the transformer

Code:
model ThreePhaseTransformerWithRectifier "Three-phase transformer (including hysteresis effect) with rectifier"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground1 ;
