modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/Transformer:
Modelica.Magnetic: Transformer1PhaseWithHysteresis (model)

Simple model of a single-phase transformer with a primary and a secondary winding and a magnetic core. The core is modeled with GenericHystTellinenEverett flux tube elements. Thus, this element considers static and dynamic hysteresis.    Fig. 1: Sketch of the modelled transformer with magnetic core, primary and secondary winding

Code:
model Transformer1PhaseWithHysteresis "Single-phase transformer with ferromagnetic core and hysteresis"
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Interfaces.NegativePin n1 "Negative pin of primary winding" ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Interfaces.PositivePin p1 "Positive pin of primary winding" ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Interfaces.NegativePin n2 "Negative pin of secondary winding" ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Interfaces.PositivePin p2 "Positive pin of secondary winding" ;
  Modelica.Thermal.HeatTransfer.Sources.PrescribedTemperature tempSource ;
  // Tab: Electrical //Group:Primary Winding
  parameter Integer N1 = 10 "Primary turns" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length L1(displayUnit = "mm") = 1.2 * 2 * (a + b) "Mean primary turn length" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length d1(displayUnit = "mm") = 0.5e-3 "Wire diameter of primary turns" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistivity rho1 = 1.678e-8 "Resistivity of primary winding (at 20degC)" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.LinearTemperatureCoefficient alpha1 = 0 "Temperature coefficient of primary turns" ;
  // Tab: Electrical //Group:Secondary Winding
  parameter Integer N2 = 10 "Secondary turns" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length L2(displayUnit = "mm") = L1 "Mean secondary turn length" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length d2(displayUnit = "mm") = d1 "Wire diameter of secondary turns" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistivity rho2 = rho1 "Resistivity of secondary winding (at 20degC)" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.LinearTemperatureCoefficient alpha2 = alpha1 "Temperature coefficient of secondary turns" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length l1(displayUnit = "mm") = 40e-3 "Mean Length l1 of core" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length l2(displayUnit = "mm") = 60e-3 "Mean Length l2 of core" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length a(displayUnit = "mm") = 15e-3 "Height of core" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length b(displayUnit = "mm") = 10e-3 "Width of core" ;
  //
  parameter Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Material.HysteresisEverettParameter.BaseData mat = Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Material.HysteresisEverettParameter.BaseData() "Parameter set of ferromagnetic Hysteresis" ;
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage v1 "Primary voltage drop";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage v2 "Secondary voltage drop";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance R1 "Primary resistance of Winding";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance R2 "Secondary resistance of Winding";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Current i1 "Primary current";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Current i2 "Secondary current";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFluxDensity B "Magnetic Flux Density of Core";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength Hstat "Ferromagnetic portion of magnetic field strength";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength Heddy "Eddy current portion of magnetic field strength";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength H "Total magnetic field strength of core";
  //output SI.Resistance R1
  parameter Real MagRelStart = 0 "Initial magnetization of Core (-1..1)" ;
  parameter Boolean MagRelFixed = false "Fixed" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength HStart = 0 "Initial magnetic field strength of Core" ;
  parameter Boolean HFixed = false "Fixed" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.ElectricCurrent I1Start = 0 "Initial primary current through winding" ;
  parameter Boolean I1Fixed = false "Fixed" ;
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power LossPowerWinding "Winding losses";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power LossPowerStat "Ferromagnetic hysteresis losses";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power LossPowerEddy "Eddy current losses";
  extends Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.ConditionalHeatPort;
  parameter Boolean EddyCurrents = false "Enable eddy currents" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Conductivity sigma = mat.sigma "Conductivity of core material" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length t(displayUnit = "mm") = 0.5e-3 "Thickness of lamination" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length L_l1 = 10e-3 "Length of leakage of primary Winding" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Area A_l1 = 10e-6 "Cross section of leakage of primary Winding" ;
  parameter Real mu_rel1 = 1 "Constant relative permeability of primary leakage (>0 required)" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length L_l2 = 10e-3 "Length of leakage of secondary Winding" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Area A_l2 = 10e-6 "Cross section of leakage of secondary Winding" ;
  parameter Real mu_rel2 = 1 "Constant relative permeability of secondary leakage (>0 required)" ;
protected
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Basic.Ground ground ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Basic.ElectroMagneticConverterWithLeakageInductance winding1(N = N1, L = L_l1, A = A_l1, mu_rel = mu_rel1, i(start = I1Start, fixed = I1Fixed)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Basic.ElectroMagneticConverterWithLeakageInductance winding2(N = N2, L = L_l2, mu_rel = mu_rel2, A = A_l2) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor1(R = rho1 * N1 * L1 / (pi / 4 * d1 ^ 2), useHeatPort = true, alpha = alpha1, T_ref = 293.15) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Resistor resistor2(R = rho2 * N2 * L2 / (pi / 4 * d2 ^ 2), useHeatPort = true, alpha = alpha2, T_ref = 293.15) ;
public
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Shapes.HysteresisAndMagnets.GenericHystTellinenEverett core(mat = mat, l = 2 * (l1 + l2), A = a * b, includeEddyCurrents = EddyCurrents, sigma = sigma, d = t, H(start = HStart, fixed = HFixed), MagRel(start = MagRelStart, fixed = MagRelFixed)) ;
equation
  v1 = p1.v - n1.v;
  i1 = resistor1.i;
  R1 = resistor1.R_actual;
  v2 = p2.v - n2.v;
  i2 = resistor2.i;
  R2 = resistor2.R_actual;
  B = core.B;
  Hstat = core.Hstat;
  Heddy = core.Heddy;
  H = core.H;
  //der(MagRel)=0;
  tempSource.T = if useHeatPort then T_heatPort else T;
  LossPowerWinding = resistor1.LossPower + resistor2.LossPower;
  //AvgWinding.y;
  LossPowerStat = core.LossPowerStat;
  LossPowerEddy = core.LossPowerEddy;
  LossPower = LossPowerWinding + LossPowerEddy + LossPowerStat;
  connect(winding1.port_n, ground.port) ;
  connect(resistor1.n, winding1.p) ;
  connect(resistor1.p, p1) ;
  connect(resistor2.n, p2) ;
  connect(winding1.n, n1) ;
  connect(tempSource.port, resistor1.heatPort) ;
  connect(resistor2.heatPort, tempSource.port) ;
  connect(winding2.port_n, ground.port) ;
  connect(winding2.n, resistor2.p) ;
  connect(n2, winding2.p) ;
  connect(core.port_p, winding1.port_p) ;
  connect(core.port_n, winding2.port_p) ;

end Transformer1PhaseWithHysteresis;

Modelica.Magnetic: Transformer3PhaseYyWithHysteresis (model)

Simple model of a three-phase transformer with primary and a secondary windings and a magnetic E-I shaped core. The core is modeled with GenericHystTellinenEverett flux tube elements. Thus, this model considers static and dynamic hysteresis as well as initial flux.    Fig. 1: Sketch of the modelled transformer with magnetic core, primary and secondary winding

Code:
model Transformer3PhaseYyWithHysteresis "Three-phase transformer in Yy configuration"
  Modelica.Thermal.HeatTransfer.Sources.PrescribedTemperature Temp ;
  // Tab: Electrical //Group:Primary Winding
  parameter Integer N1 = 10 "Primary turns" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length L1(displayUnit = "mm") = 1.2 * 2 * (a + b) "Mean primary turn length" ;
