modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/GenericHyst:
Modelica.Magnetic: GenericHysteresis (model)

Code:
partial model GenericHysteresis "Partial hysteresis model"
  extends Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.BaseClasses.Generic;
  extends Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.ConditionalHeatPort(final T = 293.15);
  parameter Boolean includeEddyCurrents = false "= true, if eddy current losses are enabled" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Conductivity sigma = 10e6 "Conductivity of core material" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length d = 0.5e-3 "Thickness of lamination" ;
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength H(start = 0) "Magnetic field strength";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength Hstat "Static (ferromagnetic) portion of the magnetic field strength";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength Heddy "Dynamic (eddy currents) portion of the magnetic field strength";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFluxDensity B "Magnetic flux density";
  output Real MagRel(final quantity = "Relative magnetization", final unit = "1", start = 0, min = -1, max = 1) "Relative magnetization at initialization (-1..1)";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power LossPowerStat "Ferromagnetic (static) hysteresis losses";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power LossPowerEddy "Eddy current losses (dynamic hysteresis losses)";
  //output SI.Power LossPower "Total power loss of core (ferromagnetic + eddy currents)"; // defined in ConditionalHeatPort
  Real derHstat(start = 0, unit = "A/(m.s)") = der(Hstat);
protected
  final parameter Real eddyCurrentFactor(final unit = "S.m") = sigma * d ^ 2 / 12;
equation
  der(MagRel) = 0;
  H = Hstat + Heddy;
  H = V_m / l;
  Phi = B * A;
  Heddy = if includeEddyCurrents then eddyCurrentFactor * der(B) else 0;
  LossPowerStat = Hstat * der(B) * V;
  LossPowerEddy = Heddy * der(B) * V;
  LossPower = LossPowerStat + LossPowerEddy;

end GenericHysteresis;

Modelica.Magnetic: GenericHysteresisTellinen (model)

A reluctance with the Tellinen hysteresis model. The major hysteresis loop is defined by the hyperbolic tangent function.   The Tellinen Hysteresis Model  
The Tellinen hysteresis model is a simple model to describe the magnetic hysteresis behavior of ferromagnetic materials. It only uses the rising (hystR) and falling (hystF) branch of the major hysteresis loop and their derivatives der(hystR) and der(hystF). See Fig. 1 and the following equations for a short description of the Tellinen hysteresis model.    diffHyst = hystF - hystR; dhR = hystF - b; dhF = b - hystR;   
if the magnetic field intensity increases (der(h)>0)    der(b) = dhR/diffHyst * der(hystR);   
if the magnetic field intensity decreases (der(h)<0)    der(b) = dhF/diffHyst * der(hystF);   

   Fig. 1: Description of the Tellinen hysteresis model.

Code:
partial model GenericHysteresisTellinen "Partial Tellinen hysteresis model"
  extends Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.BaseClasses.GenericHysteresis;
  //Real MagRel(start=0, min=-100, max=100) "Relative magnetization at initialization (-100-100%)";
  output Boolean asc(start = true) "True when der(Hstat)>0";
protected
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFluxDensity hystR "Rising branch of limiting hysteresis loop";
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFluxDensity hystF "Falling branch of limiting hysteresis loop";
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFluxDensity diffHyst "Distance between rising and falling limiting hysteresis branch at the current operating point";
  Real dHyst(final quantity = "MagneticFluxDensitySlope", final unit = "T/s") "Slope of the Rising (when der(H)>0) or Falling (when der(H)<0) limiting hysteresis branch at the current operating point";
  Real k;
  parameter Real mu0(final unit = "N/A2") = mu_0;
initial equation
  B = (hystR + hystF) / 2 + MagRel * diffHyst / 2;
equation
  asc = der(Hstat) > 0;
  der(B) = k * dHyst + mu0 * der(Hstat);
  diffHyst = hystF - hystR;
  if initial() then
    k = 0.01;
    dHyst = 0;
  elseif asc then
    dHyst = der(hystR - mu0 * Hstat);
    k = max(0.01, (hystF - B) / diffHyst);
  else
    dHyst = der(hystF - mu0 * Hstat);
    k = max(0.01, (B - hystR) / diffHyst);
  end if;

</pre></blockquote>
<p>if the magnetic field intensity decreases (der(h)&lt;0)</p>
<blockquote><pre>
der(b) = dhF/diffHyst * der(hystF);
</pre></blockquote>
<table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" border=\"0\"><tr>
<td><p><img src=\"modelica://Modelica/Resources/Images/Magnetic/FluxTubes/UsersGuide/Hysteresis/StaticHysteresis/Tellinen/TellinenDesc1.png\"/></p></td>
</tr>
</table>
<strong>Fig. 1:</strong> Description of the Tellinen hysteresis model.
</html>"));
end GenericHysteresisTellinen;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/everett:
Modelica.Magnetic: everett (function)

Code:
function everett "Everett function, see [YUY89]"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  import Modelica.Constants.pi;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength a_;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength b_;
  input Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Material.HysteresisEverettParameter.BaseData p;
  input Boolean mirror "If true then J(a,b)=-J(b,a) else J(a,b)=0 for a<b";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFluxDensity J "Magnetic polarisation";
protected
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength a;
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength b;
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength h1;
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength h2;
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength h3;
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength h4;
  constant Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFluxDensity unitT = 1;
algorithm
  if a_ >= b_ or mirror then
    a := if a_ > p.Hsat then p.Hsat elseif a_ < -p.Hsat then -p.Hsat else a_;
    b := if b_ > p.Hsat then p.Hsat elseif b_ < -p.Hsat then -p.Hsat else b_;
    h1 := -b - p.Hc;
    h2 := a - p.Hc;
    h3 := -a - p.Hc;
    h4 := b - p.Hc;
    J := unitT * ((p.M * p.r * (2 / pi * atan(p.q * h1) + 1) + 2 * p.M * (1 - p.r) / (1 + 1 / 2 * (exp(-p.p1 * h1) + exp(-p.p2 * h1)))) * (p.M * p.r * (2 / pi * atan(p.q * h2) + 1) + 2 * p.M * (1 - p.r) / (1 + 1 / 2 * (exp(-p.p1 * h2) + exp(-p.p2 * h2)))) - (p.M * p.r * (2 / pi * atan(p.q * h3) + 1) + 2 * p.M * (1 - p.r) / (1 + 1 / 2 * (exp(-p.p1 * h3) + exp(-p.p2 * h3)))) * (p.M * p.r * (2 / pi * atan(p.q * h4) + 1) + 2 * p.M * (1 - p.r) / (1 + 1 / 2 * (exp(-p.p1 * h4) + exp(-p.p2 * h4)))));
  else
    J := 0;
  end if;

end everett;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/initPreisac:
Modelica.Magnetic: initPreisach (function)

Code:
function initPreisach "Function used for the initialization of the Preisach hysteresis model GenericHystPreisachEverett"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Function;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength x;
  input Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength H;
  input Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Material.HysteresisEverettParameter.BaseData p;
  output Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFluxDensity B;
protected
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength hmax;
  Modelica.Units.SI.MagneticFieldStrength H_l;
algorithm
  H_l := if H <= -p.Hsat then -p.Hsat elseif H >= p.Hsat then p.Hsat else H;
  hmax := abs(H) + abs(x);
  B := if x < 0 then -0.5 * Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Utilities.everett(hmax, -hmax, p, false) + Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Utilities.everett(H_l, -hmax, p, false) + p.K * mu_0 * H else 0.5 * Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Utilities.everett(hmax, -hmax, p, false) - Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Utilities.everett(hmax, H_l, p, false) + p.K * mu_0 * H;
end initPreisach;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/EddyCurrent:
Modelica.Magnetic: EddyCurrentLosses (model)

In this example the eddy current losses are implemented in two different ways. Compare the loss dissipation powerb_e.power and powerb_m.power of the two models indicated by power meters.

Code:
model EddyCurrentLosses "Comparison of equivalent circuits of eddy current loss models"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  parameter Integer m = 3 "Number of phases" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance R = 0.1 "Resistance of leader cables";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Conductance Gc = 1 "Loss conductance";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Reluctance R_m = 1 "Reluctance of the magnetic circuit";
  parameter Real N = 1 "Number of turns";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power lossPower_e = sum(loss_e.conductor.LossPower);
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power lossPower_m = loss_m.lossPower;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground_e ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground_m ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Star star_e(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Star star_m(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Sources.SineVoltage sineVoltage_e(m = m, V = fill(1, m), f = fill(1, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Sources.SineVoltage sineVoltage_m(m = m, V = fill(1, m), f = fill(1, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor resistor_e(m = m, R = fill(R, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor resistor_m(m = m, R = fill(R, m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.PolyphaseElectroMagneticConverter converter_e(m = m, effectiveTurns = fill(N, m), orientation = Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.PolyphaseElectroMagneticConverter converter_m(m = m, effectiveTurns = fill(N, m), orientation = Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.Reluctance reluctance_e(R_m(d = R_m, q = R_m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.Reluctance reluctance_m(R_m(d = R_m, q = R_m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.Ground mground_e ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.Ground mground_m ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Conductor loss_e(m = m, G = fill(Gc, m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.EddyCurrent loss_m(G = m * N ^ 2 * Gc / 2) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Sensors.PowerSensor powerb_e(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Sensors.PowerSensor powerb_m(m = m) ;
initial equation
  reluctance_e.Phi = Complex(0, 0);
  reluctance_m.Phi = Complex(0, 0);
equation
  connect(sineVoltage_e.plug_n, converter_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(sineVoltage_e.plug_n, star_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(sineVoltage_m.plug_n, star_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(star_e.pin_n, ground_e.p) ;
  connect(star_m.pin_n, ground_m.p) ;
  connect(sineVoltage_m.plug_n, converter_m.plug_n) ;
  connect(converter_e.port_p, reluctance_e.port_p) ;
  connect(converter_e.port_n, reluctance_e.port_n) ;
  connect(converter_e.port_n, mground_e.port_p) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_n, reluctance_m.port_n) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_p, loss_m.port_p) ;
  connect(loss_m.port_n, reluctance_m.port_p) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_n, mground_m.port_p) ;
  connect(resistor_e.plug_p, sineVoltage_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(sineVoltage_m.plug_p, resistor_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(resistor_e.plug_n, powerb_e.pc) ;
  connect(powerb_e.pv, powerb_e.pc) ;
  connect(powerb_e.nc, loss_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(powerb_e.nv, sineVoltage_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(resistor_m.plug_n, powerb_m.pc) ;
  connect(powerb_m.pc, powerb_m.pv) ;
  connect(powerb_m.nc, converter_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(powerb_m.nv, sineVoltage_m.plug_n) ;
  connect(loss_e.plug_n, sineVoltage_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(loss_e.plug_p, converter_e.plug_p) ;

end EddyCurrentLosses;

