modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/PolyphaseIn:
Modelica.Magnetic: PolyphaseInductance (model)

This example compares an electric polyphase inductor with an equivalent fundamental wave reluctance circuit. The phase inductance L and the magnetic fundamental wave reluctance R_m are related by:     R_m = m * effectiveTurns^2 / 2 / L   
 The two currents   
resistor_e.i[1] resistor_m.i[1]  
 show the same waveforms and thus prove the equivalence of the two different modelling approaches.

Code:
model PolyphaseInductance "Polyphase inductance"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  parameter Integer m = 3 "Number of phases" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency f = 1 "Supply frequency";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage VRMS = 100 "RMS supply voltage";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance R = 0.1 "Leader cable resistance";
  parameter Real effectiveTurns = 5 "Effective number of turns";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Inductance L = 1 "Load inductance";
  final parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Reluctance R_m = m * effectiveTurns ^ 2 / 2 / L "Equivalent magnetic reluctance";
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground_e ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Analog.Basic.Ground ground_m ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Star star_e(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Star star_m(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Sources.SineVoltage voltageSource_e(m = m, f = fill(f, m), V = fill(sqrt(2) * VRMS, m), phase = -Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m) + fill(Modelica.Constants.pi / 2, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Sources.SineVoltage voltageSource_m(m = m, f = fill(f, m), V = fill(sqrt(2) * VRMS, m), phase = -Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m) + fill(Modelica.Constants.pi / 2, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor resistor_e(m = m, R = fill(R, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor resistor_m(m = m, R = fill(R, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Basic.Inductor inductor_e(m = m, L = fill(L, m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.PolyphaseElectroMagneticConverter converter_m(m = m, orientation = Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m), effectiveTurns = fill(effectiveTurns, m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.Reluctance reluctance_m(R_m(d = R_m, q = R_m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FundamentalWave.Components.Ground groundM_m ;
initial equation
  resistor_e.i = zeros(m);
  resistor_m.i[1:2] = zeros(2);
equation
  connect(star_e.plug_p, voltageSource_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(voltageSource_e.plug_n, inductor_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_p, reluctance_m.port_p) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_n, reluctance_m.port_n) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_n, groundM_m.port_p) ;
  connect(voltageSource_m.plug_n, star_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(voltageSource_m.plug_n, converter_m.plug_n) ;
  connect(voltageSource_e.plug_p, resistor_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(resistor_e.plug_n, inductor_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(voltageSource_m.plug_p, resistor_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(resistor_m.plug_n, converter_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(star_e.pin_n, ground_e.p) ;
  connect(star_m.pin_n, ground_m.p) ;

end PolyphaseInductance;

