modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/Crossing-3:
Modelica.Magnetic: Crossing (model)

This is a simple crossing of two branches. The ports port_p1 and port_p2 are connected, as well as port_n1 and port_n2 .

Code:
model Crossing "Crossing of two branches"
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.PositiveMagneticPort port_p1 "Positive port_p1 connected with port_p2" ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.PositiveMagneticPort port_p2 "Positive port_p2 connected with port_p1" ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.NegativeMagneticPort port_n1 "Negative port_n1 connected with port_n2" ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.NegativeMagneticPort port_n2 "Negative port_n2 connected with port_n1" ;
equation
  Connections.branch(port_p1.reference, port_p2.reference);
  Connections.branch(port_n1.reference, port_n2.reference);
  port_p1.reference.gamma = port_p2.reference.gamma;
  port_n1.reference.gamma = port_n2.reference.gamma;
  port_p1.V_m = port_p2.V_m;
  port_p1.Phi + port_p2.Phi = Complex(0, 0);
  port_n1.V_m = port_n2.V_m;
  port_n1.Phi + port_n2.Phi = Complex(0, 0);

end Crossing;

