modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/CoaxCylinde:
Modelica.Magnetic: CoaxCylindersEndFaces (model)

In  [Ro41]  the equations for determining the reluctance    are summarized. As an alternative to the geometry based data a  generic leakage model is provided in this library.

Code:
model CoaxCylindersEndFaces "Leakage flux between the end planes of a inner solid cylinder and a coaxial outer hollow cylinder"
  extends Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FluxTubes.BaseClasses.Leakage;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Radius r_0 = 10e-3 "Radius of inner solid cylinder" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Radius r_1 = 17e-3 "Inner radius of outer hollow cylinder";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Radius r_2 = 20e-3 "Outer radius of outer hollow cylinder";
  final parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Distance l_g = r_1 - r_0 "Radial gap length between both cylinders";
  final parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length t = r_2 - r_1 "Radial thickness of outer hollow cylinder";
equation
  // [Ro41], p. 139, Eq. (22)
  G_m = if t <= r_0 then 2 * mu_0 * (r_0 + l_g / 2) * Modelica.Math.log(1 + 2 * t / l_g) else 2 * mu_0 * (r_0 + l_g / 2) * Modelica.Math.log(1 + 2 * r_0 / l_g);

end CoaxCylindersEndFaces;

