modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/Fundamental:
Modelica.Magnetic: FundamentalWavePermabilitySensor (model)

This sensor is used to determined the effective fundamental wave permeability of a saturated lumped circuit reluctance. For this purpose the sensor is placed such way that the magnetic flux and the magnetic potential difference of the investigated reluctance are sensed. The area of cross section and the effective length of the investigated magnetic path have to be provided as parameters.   
See example  NonLinearInductor .

Code:
model FundamentalWavePermabilitySensor "Sensor of fundamental wave permeability"
  extends Modelica.Icons.RoundSensor;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency f "Fundamental wave frequency";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Area A "Area of cross section";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length l "Length";
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.PositiveMagneticPort fluxP "Positive port of flux path" ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.NegativeMagneticPort fluxN "Negative port of flux path" ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.PositiveMagneticPort potentialP "Positive port of magnetic potential difference path" ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.NegativeMagneticPort potentialN "Negative port of magnetic potential difference path" ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Sensors.MagneticPotentialDifferenceSensor magneticPotentialDifferenceSensor ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.FluxTubes.Sensors.MagneticFluxSensor magneticFluxSensor ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Harmonic harmonicPotential(final f = f, final k = 1, final x0Cos = 0, final x0Sin = 0) "Fundamental wave of magnetic potential difference" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Math.Harmonic harmonicFlux(final f = f, final k = 1, final x0Cos = 0, final x0Sin = 0) "Fundamental wave of magnetic flux" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealOutput mu(unit = "H/m") "Absolute permeability" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealOutput mur(unit = "1") "Relative permeability" ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FluxTubes.Sensors.Transient.Permeability permeability(final A = A, final l = l) "Determines relative and absolute permeability" ;
equation
  connect(magneticPotentialDifferenceSensor.port_n, potentialN) ;
  connect(magneticPotentialDifferenceSensor.port_p, potentialP) ;
  connect(magneticFluxSensor.port_p, fluxP) ;
  connect(magneticFluxSensor.port_n, fluxN) ;
  connect(harmonicFlux.u, magneticFluxSensor.Phi) ;
  connect(magneticPotentialDifferenceSensor.V_m, harmonicPotential.u) ;
  connect(permeability.V_m, harmonicPotential.y_rms) ;
  connect(permeability.Phi, harmonicFlux.y_rms) ;
  connect(permeability.mur, mur) ;
  connect(permeability.mu, mu) ;

end FundamentalWavePermabilitySensor;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/Permeabilit:
Modelica.Magnetic: Permeability (model)

This model determines the absolute and relative permeability from two real inputs:  
RMS magnetic potential difference,   RMS magnetic flux,    
In order to calculate the permeabilities, the area of cross section,   , and the geometric length,   , of the flux path have to be take into account         
In case that the magnetic potential difference is close to zero, permeabilities yield:

Code:
model Permeability "Determines permeability from flux and magnetic potential difference"
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Area A "Area of cross section penetrated by flux";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Length l "Length associated with magnetic potential difference";
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput Phi(unit = "Wb") "Magnetic flux" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealInput V_m(unit = "A") "Magnetic potential difference" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealOutput mu(unit = "H/m") "Absolute permeability" ;
  Modelica.Blocks.Interfaces.RealOutput mur(unit = "1") "Relative permeability" ;
equation
  if noEvent(abs(V_m) < Modelica.Constants.eps) then
    mu = 0;
    mur = 0;
  else
    mu = Phi / V_m * l / A;
    mur = mu / Modelica.Constants.mu_0;
  end if;

end Permeability;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/ConstantMag:
Modelica.Magnetic: ConstantMagneticPotentialDifference (model)

This source provides a constant quasi-static magnetic potential difference V_m (or magnetomotive force, mmf), at fixed frequency, f .

Code:
model ConstantMagneticPotentialDifference "Constant magnetomotive force"
  extends Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FluxTubes.Interfaces.Source;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency f(start = 1) "Frequency of the source";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexMagneticPotentialDifference V_m "Magnetic potential difference";
  Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexMagneticFlux Phi(re(start = 0), im(start = 0)) "Magnetic flux from port_p to port_n";
equation
  omega = 2 * Modelica.Constants.pi * f;
  V_m = port_p.V_m - port_n.V_m;
  Complex(0) = port_p.Phi + port_n.Phi;
  Phi = port_p.Phi;

end ConstantMagneticPotentialDifference;

