modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/PolyphaseIn:
Modelica.Magnetic: PolyphaseInductance (model)

This example compares a quasi static electric polyphase inductor with an equivalent quasi static fundamental wave reluctance circuit. The phase inductance L and the magnetic fundamental wave reluctance R_m are related by:     R_m = m * effectiveTurns^2 / 2 / L   
 The real parts   
resistor_e.i[1].re resistor_m.i[1].re  
 and the imaginary parts   
resistor_e.i[1].im resistor_m.i[1].im  
 of the two currents show the same result and thus prove the equivalence of the two different modelling approaches.

Code:
model PolyphaseInductance "Polyphase inductance"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  parameter Integer m = 5 "Number of phases" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency f = 1 "Supply frequency";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage VRMS = 100 "RMS supply voltage";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance R = 1E-5 "Resistance";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Inductance L = 1 "Load inductance";
  parameter Real effectiveTurns = 5 "Effective number of turns";
  // Symmetrical polyphase magnetic reluctance
  final parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Reluctance R_m = m * effectiveTurns ^ 2 / 2 / L "Equivalent magnetic reluctance";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexCurrent Ie = resistor_e.i[1] "Current of electric representation";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.ComplexCurrent Im = resistor_m.i[1] "Current of magnetic representation";
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.SinglePhase.Basic.Ground ground_e ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.SinglePhase.Basic.Ground ground_m ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Star star_e(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Star star_m(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Sources.VoltageSource voltageSource_e(m = m, f = f, phi = -Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m), V = fill(VRMS, m), gamma(fixed = true, start = 0)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Sources.VoltageSource voltageSource_m(m = m, f = f, phi = -Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m), V = fill(VRMS, m), gamma(fixed = true, start = 0)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor resistor_e(m = m, R_ref = fill(R * m / 3, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor resistor_m(m = m, R_ref = fill(R * m / 3, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Inductor inductor_e(m = m, L = fill(L, m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.PolyphaseElectroMagneticConverter converter_m(m = m, effectiveTurns = effectiveTurns) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.Reluctance reluctance_m(R_m(d = R_m, q = R_m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.Ground groundM_m ;
equation
  connect(star_e.pin_n, ground_e.pin) ;
  connect(star_e.plug_p, voltageSource_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(voltageSource_e.plug_n, inductor_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_p, reluctance_m.port_p) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_n, reluctance_m.port_n) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_n, groundM_m.port_p) ;
  connect(voltageSource_m.plug_n, star_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(star_m.pin_n, ground_m.pin) ;
  connect(voltageSource_m.plug_n, converter_m.plug_n) ;
  connect(voltageSource_e.plug_p, resistor_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(resistor_e.plug_n, inductor_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(voltageSource_m.plug_p, resistor_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(resistor_m.plug_n, converter_m.plug_p) ;

end PolyphaseInductance;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/EddyCurrent:
Modelica.Magnetic: EddyCurrentLosses (model)

In this example the eddy current losses are implemented in two different ways. Compare the loss dissipation powerb_e.power and powerb_m.power of the two models indicated by power meters.

Code:
model EddyCurrentLosses "Comparison of equivalent circuits of eddy current loss models"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  constant Integer m = 3 "Number of phases";
  // ## Original value R = 0.1 Ohm
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Resistance R = 0.1 "Resistance";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Conductance Gc = 0.0001 "Loss conductance";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Reluctance R_m = 1 "Reluctance of the magnetic circuit";
  parameter Real N = 1 "Number of turns";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power lossPower_e = sum(loss_e.conductor.LossPower);
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Power lossPower_m = loss_m.lossPower;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.SinglePhase.Basic.Ground ground_e ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.SinglePhase.Basic.Ground ground_m ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Star star_e(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Star star_m(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Sources.VoltageSource sineVoltage_e(m = m, f = 1, phi = -Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m), V = fill(1 / sqrt(2), m), gamma(fixed = true, start = 0)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Sources.VoltageSource sineVoltage_m(m = m, f = 1, phi = -Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m), V = fill(1 / sqrt(2), m), gamma(fixed = true, start = 0)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor resistor_e(m = m, R_ref = fill(R * m / 3, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Resistor resistor_m(m = m, R_ref = fill(R * m / 3, m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Sensors.PowerSensor powerb_e(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Sensors.PowerSensor powerb_m(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Conductor loss_e(m = m, G_ref = fill(Gc * 3 / m, m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.PolyphaseElectroMagneticConverter converter_e(effectiveTurns = N) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.PolyphaseElectroMagneticConverter converter_m(effectiveTurns = N) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.EddyCurrent loss_m(G = m * N ^ 2 * Gc / 2) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.Reluctance reluctance_e(R_m(d = R_m, q = R_m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.Reluctance reluctance_m(R_m(d = R_m, q = R_m)) ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.Ground mground_e ;
  Modelica.Magnetic.QuasiStatic.FundamentalWave.Components.Ground mground_m ;
equation
  connect(sineVoltage_e.plug_n, converter_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(sineVoltage_e.plug_n, star_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(converter_e.port_p, reluctance_e.port_p) ;
  connect(converter_e.port_n, reluctance_e.port_n) ;
  connect(converter_e.port_n, mground_e.port_p) ;
  connect(resistor_e.plug_p, sineVoltage_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(loss_e.plug_n, sineVoltage_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(loss_e.plug_p, converter_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(resistor_e.plug_n, powerb_e.currentP) ;
  connect(powerb_e.currentN, converter_e.plug_p) ;
  connect(star_e.pin_n, ground_e.pin) ;
  connect(powerb_e.currentP, powerb_e.voltageP) ;
  connect(powerb_e.voltageN, sineVoltage_e.plug_n) ;
  connect(sineVoltage_m.plug_n, star_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(sineVoltage_m.plug_n, converter_m.plug_n) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_n, reluctance_m.port_n) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_p, loss_m.port_p) ;
  connect(loss_m.port_n, reluctance_m.port_p) ;
  connect(converter_m.port_n, mground_m.port_p) ;
  connect(sineVoltage_m.plug_p, resistor_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(resistor_m.plug_n, powerb_m.currentP) ;
  connect(powerb_m.currentN, converter_m.plug_p) ;
  connect(star_m.pin_n, ground_m.pin) ;
  connect(powerb_m.currentP, powerb_m.voltageP) ;
  connect(powerb_m.voltageN, sineVoltage_m.plug_n) ;

end EddyCurrentLosses;

modelica://Modelica.Magnetic/IMC_Charact:
Modelica.Magnetic: IMC_Characteristics (model)

This examples allows the investigation of characteristic curves of quasi-static polyphase induction machines with squirrel cage rotor as a function of rotor speed.   
 Simulate for 1 second and plot (versus imcQS.wMechanical or perUnitSpeed):   
currentSensorQS.abs_i[1] : (equivalent) RMS stator current imcQS.tauElectrical : machine torque imcQS.powerBalance.powerStator : stator power imcQS.powerBalance.powerMechanical : mechanical power

Code:
model IMC_Characteristics "Characteristic curves of Induction machine with squirrel cage"
  extends Modelica.Icons.Example;
  import Modelica.Constants.pi;
  parameter Integer m = 3 "Number of phases" ;
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Voltage VsNominal = 100 "Nominal RMS voltage per phase";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.Frequency fNominal = imcData.fsNominal "Nominal frequency";
  parameter Modelica.Units.SI.AngularVelocity w_Load(displayUnit = "rev/min") = 1440.45 * 2 * Modelica.Constants.pi / 60 "Nominal load speed";
  parameter Integer p = imcData.p "Number of pole pairs";
  Real speedPerUnit = p * imcQS.wMechanical / (2 * pi * fNominal) "Per unit speed";
  Real slip = 1 - speedPerUnit "Slip";
  output Modelica.Units.SI.Current Iqs = iSensorQS.I "QS RMS current";
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Sources.VoltageSource vSourceQS(m = m, f = fNominal, V = fill(VsNominal, m), phi = -Modelica.Electrical.Polyphase.Functions.symmetricOrientation(m)) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.Polyphase.Basic.Star starQS(m = m) ;
  Modelica.Electrical.QuasiStatic.SinglePhase.Basic.Ground groundQS ;
